    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0337" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg249"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 869.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 865 of the
                    10th instant, I have the honor to inclose herewith the copy of a note which I
                    have received from <pb facs="0338" n="250" xml:id="pg250"/> the Earl of
                    Rosebery, confirming what he stated to me verbally relative to the recognition
                    of our commercial agency at Butaritari, in the Gilbert Islands, and expressing
                    the regret of Her Majesty’s Government that Capt. Davis, of H. M. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Royalist</hi>, did not provisionally recognize Mr. Rick
                    in that capacity.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d192-a1.xml" xpointer="d192-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
